{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-dfe19022024b38a95656","statement":"A semi-perfect noetherian algebra $\\bA$ is called nodal if it is pure noetherian (i.e. has no minimal ideals), and there is a hereditary algebra $\\bH\\supseteq\\bA$, which is semi-perfect and pure noetherian such that\n\n- $\\rad \\bA=\\rad \\bH$.\n\n- $\\lenght_{\\bA}(\\bH\\otimes_{\\bA}U)\\leq 2$ for every simple left $\\bA$-module $U$.\n\n- $\\lenght_{\\bA}(V\\otimes_{\\bA}\\bH)\\leq 2$ for every simple right $\\bA$-module $V$.","source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"bd880a5f088223217213a29f01ed0bb455407ea788865800b77e6b883fa6f73c","kind":"definition","label":"Definition 2","ref_key":"noddef","name":"","order":4,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"4691b7e6310aff594015f4ee9295f0c5d77eb87af5ba0a297bb3f4cdbb2ee258","line":322,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:07+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":408,"math_hints":45}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","title":"Derived tame local and two-point algebras","abstract":"We determine derived representation type of complete finitely generated local and two-point algebras over an algebraically closed field.","authors":["Viktor Bekkert","Yuriy Drozd","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2008","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"lenght":"\\mathop\\mathrm{lenght}\\nolimits","md":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{mod}","pr":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{pro}","bp":"\\bullet","iso":"\\simeq","iff":"if and only if","setsuch":"\\left\\{\\,#1\\,|\\,#2\\,\\right\\}","rad":"\\mathop\\mathrm{rad}","End":"\\mathop\\mathrm{End}","im":"\\mathop\\mathrm{Im}","al":"\\alpha","be":"\\beta","la":"\\lambda","Si":"\\Sigma","bA":"\\mathbf A","bB":"\\